iginally as {Leah_num}.\nHer sister had {sister_num} chocolates originally.\nSo in total they had {all_num} = {Leah_num} + {sister_num} chocolates originally.\nAfter eating {eating_num} chocolates, the number of chocolates they have left {remain_num} is {all_num} minus {eating_num}.\nThe answer is {remain_num} = {all_num} - {eating_num}.\n\n## Actual analysis and solution process\n\nIn this question, {Leah_num} = 32, {sister_num} = 42 and {eating_num} = 35.\nSo, in total they had 32 + 42 = 74 chocolates originally.\nAfter eating 35 chocolates, they had 74 - 35 = 39 chocolates.\nThe answer is 39.\n\n## Problem solving process analysis\n\nLet's denote the distance the grasshopper jumped as {grasshopper_jump} inches.\nThe distance the frog jumped is 33 inches farther than the grasshopper, so the frog jumped {frog_jump} = {grasshopper_jump} + 33 inches.\nThe distance the mouse jumped is 3 inches lesser than the frog, so the mouse jumped {mouse_jump} = {frog_jump} - 3 inches.\nThe answer is {mouse_jump} = {frog_jump} - 3.\n\n## Actual analysis and solution process\n\nIn this question, {grasshopper_jump} = 9 and {frog_jump} = 33 + 9 = 42.\nSo, the mouse jumped 42 - 3 = 39 inches.\nThe answer is 39."], "Programming ExpertRMBb": ["```python\n\ndef mouse_jump_distance():\n    grasshopper_jump = 9\n    frog_jump = grasshopper_jump + 33\n    mouse_jump = frog_jump - 3\n    return mouse_jump\n\nanswer = mouse_jump_distance()\n\n```\nthe answer is 39"], "Inspector5BpJ": ["The analysis and solution process of both Agent UHMC and Agent qwBd are correct.\n\nHere's my own solving process step by step based on the hints:\n\n1. The grasshopper jumped 9 inches.\n2. The frog jumped 33 inches farther than the grasshopper, so the frog jumped 9 + 33 = 42 inches.\n3. The mouse jumped 3 inches lesser than the frog, so the mouse jumped 42 - 3 = 39 inches.\n\nThe answer is 39."], "Math SolverqwBd": ["Q: The grasshopper, the frog and the mouse had a jumping contest. The grasshopper jumped 9 inc